    "summary": "High‑energy Other One marathon, epic Good Lovin’ and tender Brokedown Palace",
    "blurb": "The second set launches into a high‑energy The Other One → Sitting on Top of the World sequence followed by an 18‑minute Good Lovin’. Highlights also include a stellar Brokedown Palace and strong performances of Truckin’, Comes A Time and Not Fade Away.",
    "review": "December 10, 1971 at St. Louis' Fox Theatre finds the Dead in top form as they roll from a solid first set into a blistering second‑set marathon. The band erupts with an electrifying The Other One → Sitting on Top of the World sandwich that stretches and contracts with Jerry’s soaring leads and Phil’s booming bass, while Keith’s sweet piano adds jazzy color. An 18‑minute Good Lovin’ showcases relentless drive, leading into a beautifully rendered Brokedown Palace before the group rides through Truckin’, Not Fade Away and a heartfelt Comes A Time. The rhythm section—Bill Kreutzmann's tight drumming and Phil’s “bombs” on bass—keeps everything locked in, and Bob Weir steps forward vocally, adding depth to the more upbeat numbers. This full‑show soundboard capture preserves every nuance of an unforgettable night.",
